---
layout: sidebar-layout.njk
---
{% from "about-content.njk" import aboutContent %}

{# Standalone permalink route for one About section (/about/bio/, /about/timeline/, ...).

   These exist as direct-linkable targets; the primary presentation is the homepage's
   About tabs, which render exactly the same content through the shared aboutContent
   macro in about-content.njk - one source of truth for the markup.

   No quick-switcher nav here on purpose: the sidebar already links each of these (as
   homepage tab anchors), and the site's model is sidebar-fixed / content-switches-in-place
   via tabs, not page-to-page navigation between sibling pages - same pattern as individual
   project pages, which also have no redundant category-switcher of their own. #}

<article class="page-content about-subpage">
    <div class="about-section-shell">
        {# Bio's opening paragraph lives in `excerpt`, because on the homepage it renders
           beside the portrait above the tab bar (per Figma, the Bio panel itself starts at
           paragraph 2). This standalone route has no intro block, so the excerpt is shown
           here as a lead - otherwise the page would start mid-biography. Only applies to
           the prose sections; the structured ones use `excerpt` as a summary, not as copy. #}
        {% if excerpt and not timelineSections and not linkCategories and not pressEntries %}
            <p class="about-lead">{{ excerpt }}</p>
        {% endif %}

        {{ aboutContent({
            timelineSections: timelineSections,
            linkCategories: linkCategories,
            linksHeading: linksHeading,
            pressEntries: pressEntries,
            pressNote: pressNote
        }, content) }}
    </div>
</article>
